\item Bricken et al.\ used Claude 2: show it examples of text with the feature's activations (mostly top activations, plus examples from other activation ranges and random ones)
\item Claude writes an explanation
\item Then, given only the explanation, Claude predicts the activations on unseen text
\item Score: Spearman correlation between predicted and true activations
\item A good score means the label explains the feature's behavior, not that it captures everything the feature does
