\note{
\begin{itemize}
\item The mental model for everything in this section
\item The residual stream carries the activation through the model. Each attention layer and MLP reads from it (a linear projection) and writes back by adding
\item So the final logits are a sum over the contributions of all components: we can attribute the output to individual heads, and patch individual contributions
\item Attention heads split into two independent pieces: the QK circuit decides where to attend, the OV circuit decides what information is moved
\item MLPs act per position: they read the stream and write new features back
\end{itemize}
}
\end{frame}

