\begin{itemize}
\item Cross-layer transcoder: each feature reads from the residual stream at the input to the MLP in layer $\ell$ (linear encoder + JumpReLU)
\item It contributes to the MLP outputs of all later layers, with a separate decoder per layer
\item Local replacement model for one prompt: swap the MLPs for the CLT, take the attention patterns and normalization denominators from the real forward pass, add error nodes for the difference between true MLP output and CLT output (error nodes have no input edges)
\item Edge weight: source activation times the virtual weight, i.e.\ the derivative of the target's preactivation with respect to the source with all nonlinearities stop-gradiented
\item Because everything nonlinear is frozen, the graph is linear and edges add up exactly
\item Pruning: keep nodes responsible for $\sim$80\% of the influence on the logits and edges for $\sim$98\%
\end{itemize}
